The Jenkins logs present in the EFS are 1:1 with the builds in Jenkins - currently there is no enforcement on keeping a certain amount of build logs per job (configurable in the Jenkins multibranch jobs) - I think it is ok to remove all the PR stale branches as long as they are not currently present in Jenkins - so when u remove the "stale" workspaces make sure there are no equivalent jobs in Jenkins for them (if there are - it is possible that removing the logs older than 90 days - they won't show up in Jenkins console anymore) - also there has been restructuring of jobs in Jenkins by a few teams - it is worth while to match them up and remove the stale folders
